# 0093-r5-review-fixes.patch -- the third-party review r5 (2026-11-22) on patches 0078-0091: each point checked against the code, fixed here. Applies after 0092.
# UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# P3 (0090 RemoteReadStream) CONFIRMED: a remote read that gave nothing (or ended early) left a SHORT block in the cache as if it were whole, so a Read could still end before the end of the
#    file. A block is now cached only whole (the last one as long as the listed size says); an empty reply is tried again from where it stopped, MaxEmptyReads (3) times in a row, then the
#    read fails with a clear IOException ("the remote file gave nothing at byte N of its listed M (3 tries): it is shorter than listed, or the connection stalled"); a file shorter than
#    listed is that error now (it was "what there is"). GameAppWarm.cs's pack header (GameWarmLogic.ReadImageIndex) was ONE Read of 32 bytes: ReadAtLeast now. Every other Read of a stream
#    where a full count is assumed loops already (checked: GameAppWarm.cs 83/268/838, GameAppUi.cs, GameAppDiag.cs, GameAppBootOverlay.cs, the NupRemote callback, the copies).
# P7 (0085 free space) CONFIRMED in part: kept the important-use figure for decisions AND display (Apple's figure for work the person asked for: the main agent's decision); but a failed
#    `new DriveInfo(Documents)` became a silent 0. Now: DriveInfo, else statfs on Documents (struct statfs of Darwin arm64: f_bsize at 0, f_bavail at 24), else UNKNOWN (-1): an unknown
#    figure refuses nothing (DiskSpace.Refuses: the download's and the export's checks), is shown as "unknown", and the log says "free space unknown: …".
# P8 (0087 GameWarm.Start) CONFIRMED: the next run's thread joins the stopped one's for at most 5 s (WarmRun.JoinTimeoutMs), then abandons it with a log line (it stops at its next library:
#    its run number is not current) and goes on. The join is on the run's own thread, never the main one.
# P9 (0088 PartialDiscard.Plan) CONFIRMED: a paused REBUILD of a game whose finished build is still in Documents (the framework stamp names it, for this app build) lost its stamp and
#    framework at a discard. Now only the rebuild's shader work folder goes (extract/, the framework, its stamp, the marker and profile.tsv are that build's and stay), and the question says
#    "Removes what the paused rebuild made so far…; Its finished build stays: it still plays."; "Not built" is said only of a game that is not built.
# P18 (0083 playStopped) CONFIRMED: the "Play was stopped before the game started" line was cleared only by the next Play: now by ANY run's start (a build too) and by its game's delete.
# P19 (weak points): 0080's comment on LibraryActions.Enabled said "the two" buttons stay on while busy; the code (since 0085) keeps three: the comment is fixed (the code is right).
#    0086 QueuePlan.For(Paused) = Add: kept (a paused game may be queued), and made coherent: the queue now RESUMES a paused game from where it stopped (StartQueued: ResumePlan, the files
#    kept in extract/, as Resume; from the start with the cache only when a run already came back in this process), its queue row says "Resume", its menu entry "Queue the resume"; Resume
#    and "Discard the partial build" stay its own entries. 0078 "Rebuild, or send the log" was a build's words: a PLAY refused for no shader library now says "The game was not started: its
#    shader library is missing and could not be made again (it would draw nothing). Play again; if it fails again, rebuild the game, or send the log." (log line, notification).
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch 0010-0093 applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile
#   (-t:Compile): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness93: … P91;P93): 342 of 342 checks (20 new: a 0-byte reply then data, short and empty
#   replies mid-file over 300 random reads, the end of file exactly, a file shorter than listed, bounded retries, the pack header, unknown free space, statfs's layout MEASURED on this Mac
#   (statfs = DriveInfo to the byte), the join timeout, the rebuild's discard, the words, playStopped, the queue's resume, the Play's words, the comment); 14 of 14 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: statfs on iOS (same arm64 struct as the Mac's, by the SDK header), a real stalled SFTP reply, a real queued resume.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "unknown", "Queue the resume", "Resume", ChainResult.NoShaderLibraryPlayText, PartialDiscard.KeepsBuilt, "Removes what the paused rebuild made so far"; log lines
#   "free space unknown: ", "the remote file gave nothing at byte ", "did not end within ", "build queue: … was paused: it goes on from where it stopped".
